# Chaos: head accessories sit on the head of the body they are drawn with (O561; client/BASE.md "0200"; src/client/chaosheadfit.h
# (new, pure), outfit.cpp, luafunctions_client.cpp; after 0001-0199).
# Owner report 2026-11-14: "most helmets are off plumb too". A head accessory (the pair 33 head pieces, auras 2477-2568) is an
# aura look, drawn at the creature's place, and its art was placed against one body, the stock look 128. A class look has its
# head elsewhere (median 2 px left of and 4 px above look 128's facing south, p10 to p90 -5.5 to +1.1 and -12 to -1), so the piece
# sat beside the head. Now Outfit::draw adds head(body) - head(look 128) to the piece's destination, both layers, per direction,
# from one table the module client_chaos_wingfit hands in (setOutfitHeadCentre, setOutfitHeadRef, setOutfitHeadPieces,
# clearOutfitHeadCentres; made from the pair by client/tools/sprites/gen_wing_centres.py). No row, an aura outside the piece
# range, or a mounted rider: no shift (the draw as before).
diff -ru a/src/client/chaosheadfit.h b/src/client/chaosheadfit.h
